A||||10||alpha||What can a Fiero tow?||||1||
Z||000000||alpha||06-11-2001||09:04 PM||||I am in the process of purchasing a Formula Vee... I will need to tow it. I am going to build a custom trailer for it.<P>My question is can a Fiero (85 GT auto) tow that kind of weight (~2000 lbs with trailer and spares) safely if I keep the tounge weight down?<P>I know Ed Parks has towed many Fieros with a Fiero, but I am not sure if this is a good idea or not.<P>--Doug Knight||||reg||1
Z||000001||KissMySSFiero||06-11-2001||10:11 PM||||ok maybe im an idiot...but whats a formula vee?<P>i towed a uhaul trailer(4x8 enclosed) just over 1000 miles from jacksonville fla to NW indiana by chicago.  no problems at all.  only got about 15mpg.  but i was able to cruise around 75-80 with any problems.  even went past 90 before i noticed.  i have a 5spd formula with 160k miles.  i dont know how well your engine was maintained but my brother owned my car before me.  he had it since 92 with 30k miles.  did all maintenance on time as did i.  only recently have i seen any kind of blowby on start up.  and its not even every time.  i dont knwo what the difference would be towing with an auto as opposed to a manual but im sure you could do it.  <BR>only thing that sucks is backing up.. ugh.<BR><P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan||06-11-2001||10:49 PM|||| I towed my one ton Ford van home with my 85 4 cylinder coupe one time. Damnest sight hundreds ever saw.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||06-12-2001||01:27 AM||||So the total weight of the car & trailer is about 2000 pounds?  That is definitley doable.  I have successfully towed many cars (mostly Fieros) with an auto. '88 GT.  I even towed a Saturn cross country (Portland, OR to Portland, ME) with no real problems.  <P>I too averaged 15MPG, but that isn't too bad.  I estimate the total weight of my dolly and the car at about 3500 pounds, so 2000 should be a breeze. <P>The only thing you need to worry about is stopping.  The '88 brakes are less prone to fading, so I didn't have much to worry about as far as stopping.  I suggest down shifting to L2 then L1 when you approach a stop.....let the engine do most of the work for you.<P><BR>If you'll be at the OOB, Maine show this weekend I'll show you a picture of my GT loaded with the dolly and a 2000 Saturn (also had a complete 3.4 V-6 in the passenger seat area!).  What a sight!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||JSocha||06-12-2001||09:06 AM||||Just thinking about Dan's post and then it got me to thinking about, I believe its the Chevy commercial.  Sure you may have seen it.<P>Wouldn't it have been cool to see instead of the Chevy pickup truck, to see instead a Fiero pulling up in front of that stahled 18 wheeler in the commercial and have the owner of the Fiero tell the truck driver to make sure it was in Neutral?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
